      "title": "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem and the Rank-Nullity Theorem"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "bd663282-9f7f-55d0-8400-1696173736bf",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix with $5$ pivot columns?\n\nI. $\\text{rank}(A)=4$\n\nII. $A$ is not invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$\\,\u21d4\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{5} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe 5 pivot columns give $\\text{rank}(A)=5.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n5+\\text{nullity}(A)=5,\\qquad \\text{nullity}(A)=5-5=0.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=5$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$. Since rank equals the number of columns, $A$ is invertible and $\\det(A)\\ne 0$. Also, $\\text{Col}(A)$ has dimension 5. The number of pivot columns is 5, and the number of non-pivot columns is 0.\n\n- Statement I is false. $\\text{rank}(A)=5$.\n\n- Statement II is false. The rank equals the number of columns.\n\n- Statement III is true. $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is III only.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "50e312fc-3eb8-5534-bc40-ce462a5df0fd",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/correct": [
