  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186184172,
      "id": "5e145cb2-806a-579d-8299-8a91a6feaad1",
      "title": "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem and the Rank-Nullity Theorem"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b05d8431-efb6-5d68-9b90-0e12695521c9",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $14\\times 14$ matrix which has only $3$ non-pivot column?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $14\\times 14$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$$\n\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{14} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=14=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe 3 non-pivot columns give $\\text{nullity}(A)=3.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+3=14,\\qquad \\text{rank}(A)=14-3=11.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=11$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=3$. Since rank is less than the number of columns, $A$ is not invertible and $\\det(A)=0$. Also, $\\text{Col}(A)$ has dimension 11. The number of pivot columns is 11, and the number of non-pivot columns is 3.\n\n- Statement \u201c$A$ is not invertible\u201d is true. The rank is less than the number of columns.\n\n- Statement \u201c$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $4$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{14}.$\u201d is false. $\\dim(\\text{Col}(A))=11$.\n\n- Statement \u201c$\\text{nullity}(A)=1$\u201d is false. $\\text{nullity}(A)=3$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A$ is not invertible.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
