  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186184172,
      "id": "5e145cb2-806a-579d-8299-8a91a6feaad1",
      "title": "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem and the Rank-Nullity Theorem"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e3fac3e3-3f17-5455-8fd8-11326a48f02a",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix with $1$ pivot columns?\n\nI. $\\text{rank}(A)=1$\n\nII. $A$ is not invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{nullity}(A)=3$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$\\,\u21d4\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe 1 pivot columns give $\\text{rank}(A)=1.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n1+\\text{nullity}(A)=4,\\qquad \\text{nullity}(A)=4-1=3.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=1$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=3$. Since rank is less than the number of columns, $A$ is not invertible and $\\det(A)=0$. Also, $\\text{Col}(A)$ has dimension 1. The number of pivot columns is 1, and the number of non-pivot columns is 3.\n\n- Statement I is true. $\\text{rank}(A)=1$.\n\n- Statement II is true. The rank is less than the number of columns.\n\n- Statement III is true. $\\text{nullity}(A)=3$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is I, II, and III.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
