    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7cf18673-630f-5823-bf8a-a9a34c953765",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $10\\times 10$ matrix with $2$ pivot columns?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $10\\times 10$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$$\n\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{10} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=10=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe 2 pivot columns give $\\text{rank}(A)=2.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n2+\\text{nullity}(A)=10,\\qquad \\text{nullity}(A)=10-2=8.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=2$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=8$. Since rank is less than the number of columns, $A$ is not invertible and $\\det(A)=0$. Also, $\\text{Col}(A)$ has dimension 2. The number of pivot columns is 2, and the number of non-pivot columns is 8.\n\n- Statement \u201c$A$ is invertible\u201d is false. The rank is less than the number of columns.\n\n- Statement \u201c$\\text{nullity}(A)=8$\u201d is true. $\\text{nullity}(A)=8$.\n\n- Statement \u201c$\\text{rank}(A)=2$\u201d is true. $\\text{rank}(A)=2$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{nullity}(A)=8$; $\\text{rank}(A)=2$.",
